# 📘 Project 2.0 (KUDAY) Backend - Master Architecture & Technical Guide

This document is your complete, step-by-step technical guide to the Project 2.0 (KUDAY) backend. It details every architectural layer, implemented feature, database model, external infrastructure service, security mechanism, and API endpoint.

---

## 🏛️ System Architecture Overview

The backend is engineered with **Clean Architecture** (4 strictly decoupled layers) and adheres to **SOLID Principles**:

```
backend/src/
├── domain/                  # 1. Core business entities & mathematical algorithms (Zero external dependencies)
│   ├── entities/            # Pure TypeScript contracts (UserEntity, RoomEntity, LifestyleEntity, etc.)
│   └── services/            # Pure domain algorithms (RoomMatchCalculatorService)
├── application/             # 2. Business use cases & abstract interfaces
│   ├── interfaces/          # Repository, service, and use case contracts (IUserRepository, IJwtService)
│   ├── dto/                 # Data Transfer Objects defining request/response structures
│   ├── errors/              # Domain & application-specific error classes (ApplicationError, NotFoundError, etc.)
│   └── use-case/            # Single-responsibility workflows (auth, user, room, admin, seeker, notification)
├── infrastructure/          # 3. External tools, database, and third-party integrations
│   ├── database/            # MongoDB connection & Mongoose schemas (UserModel, OtpModel, etc.)
│   ├── repository/          # Concrete database repositories implementing domain interfaces
│   ├── services/            # Cloudinary, Nodemailer, Bcrypt, JWT, and Crypto OTP generators
│   ├── di/                  # Composition Root & Dependency Injection container (AppFactory.ts)
│   └── logging/             # Structured logging utilities
└── presentation/            # 4. HTTP delivery layer (Express Web / API)
    ├── controller/          # Request handlers reading req.body/params and sending standardized JSON
    ├── router/              # Express route declarations with middleware binding
    ├── middleware/          # JWT authentication guard & Centralized Error Handler
    └── utils/               # ApiResponse wrapper, HttpStatusCodes enums, and Zod validator schemas
```

---

## 🗄️ Database Models (`src/infrastructure/database/model`)

All models are constructed using **Modern Mongoose (`InferSchemaType` + `HydratedDocument`)** providing a single source of type truth:

1. **`UserModel.ts`**:
   - **Authentication**: `email` (unique, lowercase, trimmed index), `hashedPassword`, `otp`.
   - **Personal Info**: `firstName`, `lastName`, `dob`, `gender`, `occupation`, `bio`.
   - **Account Status**: `isVerified` (boolean), `isBlocked` (boolean), `isAdmin` (boolean), `isOnboarded` (boolean).
   - **Role Management**: `role` (`"host"` | `"seeker"` | `"admin"` | `"none"`).
   - **Identity Verification**: `idCardUrl` (Cloudinary CDN), `selfieUrl` (Cloudinary CDN), `identityVerified` (boolean), `identityStatus` (`"pending"` | `"verified"` | `"rejected"` | `"none"`), `rejectionReason`.

2. **`OtpModel.ts`**:
   - **Fields**: `email` (`index: true`), `otp` (number), `expiresAt`, `createdAt`.
   - **Database Optimization**: MongoDB **TTL Index** (`expires: 600`) that automatically purges expired OTP documents from database memory after 10 minutes without requiring cron jobs.

3. **`RoomModel.ts`**:
   - **Fields**: `userId` (`index: true`), `title`, `roomType`, `monthlyRent`, `location`, `capacity`, `availabilityNotes`, `amenities`, `images` (Cloudinary CDN URLs array), `description`, `isActive`.

4. **`SeekerPreferenceModel.ts`**:
   - **Fields**: `userId` (`index: true`), `preferredLocation`, `maxBudget`, `roomTypePreference`, `requiredAmenities`, `isActive`.

5. **`LifestyleModel.ts`**:
   - **Fields**: `userId` (ref to User), `smoking`, `drinking`, `sleepSchedule`, `diet`, `cleanliness`, `visitorPolicy`, `roommateGenderPref`.

6. **`NotificationModel.ts`**:
   - **Fields**: `userId` (`index: true`), `title`, `message`, `type` (`"admin_verification"` | `"interest_request"` | `"system"`), `isRead`.

---

## 🚀 Complete Feature Breakdown

### 1. Authentication & Security Module (`src/application/use-case/auth/`)
* **User Registration (`SignUpUserUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Validates user input with Zod (`RegisterUserSchema`).
  - Checks if an active verified account exists. If unverified, deletes previous OTP sessions.
  - Hashes passwords using `bcrypt` (10 salt rounds).
  - Generates a cryptographically secure 6-digit OTP code (`OtpServices.ts`).
  - Dispatches an HTML verification email via `nodemailer` (Gmail SMTP).
* **OTP Verification (`VerifyOtpUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Verifies code validity and expiration against `OtpModel`.
  - Marks `isVerified = true` and purges the used OTP document.
  - Issues a signed 7-day JWT access token.
* **User Login (`LoginUserUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Validates credentials and verifies user existence.
  - Enforces account status checks (`isBlocked`, `isVerified`).
  - Compares password against stored bcrypt hash.
  - Returns access token, user metadata, onboarding status, and role info.
* **Silent Token Refresh (`RefreshTokenUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Verifies incoming refresh token from `httpOnly` secure cookie.
  - Generates a fresh JWT access token without forcing the user to log in again.
* **Forgot Password Flow (`ForgotPasswordUseCase.ts`, `VerifyResetOtpUseCase.ts`, `ResetPasswordUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Dispatches password reset OTP to user's inbox.
  - Verifies reset OTP and authorizes password change.
  - Safely updates hashed password in database.
* **Google OAuth (`GoogleAuthUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Supports one-click Google Sign-in / Sign-up with email verification bypass.

---

### 2. User Onboarding & Profile System (`src/application/use-case/user/`)
* **Profile Management (`UpdateProfileUseCase.ts`, `GetUserProfileUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Updates personal details (gender, occupation, bio, DOB).
  - **Date of Birth Guard**: Enforces that DOB cannot be set to a future date.
  - **Mass-Assignment Protection**: Repository restricts updates strictly to `PROFILE_UPDATABLE_FIELDS`, protecting administrative and sensitive flags (`isAdmin`, `isBlocked`, `hashedPassword`).
* **Lifestyle Habits (`CreateLifestyleUseCase.ts`, `GetLifestyleUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Captures 7 living habits: smoking, drinking, diet, sleep schedule, cleanliness, visitor policy, and gender preference.
* **Identity Verification Upload (`UploadIdentityUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Accepts base64 encoded Government ID Card and Selfie camera capture.
  - Uploads securely to Cloudinary CDN (`kuday_id_cards`, `kuday_selfies`).
  - Sets `identityStatus = "pending"` for Admin review and dispatches a confirmation notification.
* **Dual-Role Switching (`UpdateRoleUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Enables users to seamlessly switch between **Host** and **Seeker** modes.
  - **Post Invalidation**: When a user switches roles, their active listing in the opposite role is automatically deactivated (`isActive = false`) to maintain marketplace integrity.
* **Password Change (`ChangePasswordUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Allows authenticated users to change their password by validating old credentials.

---

### 3. Property & Room Listings (`src/application/use-case/room/`)
* **Room Creation & Upload (`CreateRoomUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Hosts list rooms with rent, location, capacity, house rules, and amenities.
  - Automatically uploads multiple property photos to Cloudinary CDN (`kuday_rooms`).
* **Verified Room Discovery (`GetRoomsUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Fetches active rooms listed by **Admin-Verified hosts**.
  - Cross-references current seeker's preferences and lifestyle habits.
  - Dynamically runs the **Compatibility Engine** and returns listings sorted by match score.

---

### 4. Roommate Seeker Preferences (`src/application/use-case/seeker/`)
* **Preference Management (`CreateSeekerPreferenceUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Seekers specify target location, maximum budget, room type, and required amenities.
* **Seeker Discovery for Hosts (`GetSeekerPreferencesUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Hosts can browse verified roommate seekers.
  - Evaluates match scores between host's room specifications and seeker requirements.

---

### 5. Domain Compatibility Match Engine (`src/domain/services/RoomMatchCalculatorService.ts`)
A dedicated, zero-dependency mathematical algorithm calculating a **0% to 100% compatibility rating**:
* **Location Match (25% Weight)**: Case-insensitive substring matching between room address and seeker preference.
* **Budget Match (25% Weight)**: 100% points if rent $\le$ max budget; partial score if within 10% budget flexibility.
* **Room Type Match (15% Weight)**: Exact match or seeker preference set to `"any"`.
* **Amenities Match (15% Weight)**: Overlap ratio between seeker's required amenities and room's provided amenities.
* **Lifestyle Compatibility (20% Weight)**: Detailed scoring across cleanliness, sleep schedule, smoking, and drinking habits.

---

### 6. Admin Portal & Verification Queue (`src/application/use-case/admin/`)
* **Admin Login (`AdminLoginUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Dedicated admin authentication checking `isAdmin === true`.
* **Identity Document Verification Queue (`VerifyUserIdentityUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Admin inspects submitted Government ID and Selfie photos side-by-side.
  - **Approve**: Sets `identityVerified = true`, `identityStatus = "verified"`.
  - **Reject**: Sets `identityVerified = false`, `identityStatus = "rejected"`, and records a mandatory `rejectionReason`.
  - Dispatches an automated in-app notification to the user detailing the outcome and reason.
* **User Management & Moderation (`GetAllUsersUseCase.ts`, `ToggleBlockUserUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Real-time user directory with search and role filters.
  - Instant account blocking/unblocking with immediate session revocation.
* **System Analytics (`GetAdminStatsUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Aggregates platform KPIs: Total Users, Active Rooms, Verified Hosts, and Pending Verifications.

---

### 7. In-App Notification System (`src/application/use-case/notification/`)
* **Dispatches real-time alerts**:
  - `"interest_request"`: Dispatched when a user expresses interest in a room or roommate.
  - `"admin_verification"`: Dispatched when an admin approves or rejects identity documents.
  - `"system"`: Platform announcements.
* **Endpoints**: Retrieve notifications by user ID, mark individual notification as read, or mark all as read.

---

### 8. Connection & Interest Management (`src/application/use-case/interest/`)
* **Send Interest (`SendInterestUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Validates sender $\ne$ receiver.
  - Enforces compound uniqueness (`senderId + receiverId + targetId`) so duplicate requests cannot be spammed.
  - Dispatches an automated in-app notification to the recipient.
* **Accept Interest (`UpdateInterestStatusUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Verifies that only the designated recipient can approve.
  - Sets `status = "accepted"`.
  - Dispatches celebration notification to the sender confirming connection and revealing mutual contact details.
* **Decline Interest (`UpdateInterestStatusUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Sets `status = "declined"`.
* **Received & Sent Lists (`GetReceivedInterestsUseCase.ts`, `GetSentInterestsUseCase.ts`)**:
  - Fetches populated sender and receiver profiles for dashboard display.

---

### 9. Dependency Injection & Clean Composition Root (`src/infrastructure/di/AppFactory.ts`)
* All service instantiations, repository bindings, use-case injections, and controller setups are centralized inside [`AppFactory.ts`](file:///c:/Users/ASUS/Desktop/Project2.0/backend/src/infrastructure/di/AppFactory.ts).
* Keeps [`server.ts`](file:///c:/Users/ASUS/Desktop/Project2.0/backend/src/server.ts) lean and focused solely on HTTP server bootstrap and middleware registration.

---

### 9. Centralized Error Handling & Validation Layer
* **`ErrorHandlerMiddleware.ts`**:
  - Automatically catches and maps `ApplicationError`, `ZodError`, `JsonWebTokenError`, and MongoDB duplicate-key errors (`11000`).
  - Shields internal stack traces in production while sending clear, formatted error messages to the client.
* **`ApiResponse.ts` & `HttpStatusCodes.ts`**:
  - Standardizes all JSON payloads: `{ success: boolean, message: string, data?: T, error?: string }`.
* **Zod Schemas (`presentation/utils/validators/zod/`)**:
  - Strong runtime validation across Auth, Profile, Lifestyle, Room, and Seeker inputs.

---

## 🔌 External Infrastructure Services (`src/infrastructure/services/`)

| Service File | Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `CloudinaryService.ts` | Cloudinary SDK v2 | Uploads base64 encoded images to secure cloud CDN and returns optimized HTTPS URLs. |
| `JwtServices.ts` | `jsonwebtoken` | Generates and verifies signed HMAC SHA-256 JWT access and refresh tokens. |
| `HashingService.ts` | `bcrypt` | Hashes passwords with 10 salt rounds and securely compares plaintext passwords with stored hashes. |
| `NodemailerService.ts` | `nodemailer` (Gmail SMTP) | Connects to SMTP email relay to send formatted HTML OTP emails to users. |
| `OtpServices.ts` | Node.js `crypto` | Generates cryptographically secure 6-digit numeric OTP tokens. |
| `Logger.ts` | Custom Winston / Console Logger | Formatted timestamped logging for operational monitoring. |

