## 📡 API Endpoints Reference

### 1. Authentication (`/auth`)
| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `POST` | `/auth/signUp` | Register user & dispatch OTP email |
| `POST` | `/auth/verify-otp` | Verify 6-digit OTP & issue JWT access token |
| `POST` | `/auth/login` | Login with email and password |
| `POST` | `/auth/refresh-token` | Renew access token via httpOnly cookie |
| `POST` | `/auth/forgot-password` | Request password reset OTP email |
| `POST` | `/auth/verify-reset-otp` | Verify reset OTP |
| `POST` | `/auth/reset-password` | Save new password |
| `POST` | `/auth/google` | Google OAuth sign-in / registration |

### 2. User & Onboarding (`/users`)
| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `GET` | `/users/profile/:userId` | Get profile details and verification status |
| `PUT` | `/users/profile` | Update personal profile information |
| `PUT` | `/users/role` | Switch between Host and Seeker roles |
| `POST` | `/users/upload-identity` | Upload ID Card & Selfie for admin verification |
| `POST` | `/users/change-password` | Change password for authenticated user |

### 3. Lifestyle (`/lifestyles`)
| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `POST` | `/lifestyles` | Create or update user living habits |
| `GET` | `/lifestyles/:userId` | Retrieve user lifestyle preferences |

### 4. Room Listings (`/rooms`)
| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `POST` | `/rooms` | Create property listing with Cloudinary images |
| `GET` | `/rooms?userId=:userId` | Fetch verified rooms with dynamic match scores |
| `GET` | `/rooms/host/:hostId` | Fetch room listings for a specific host |

### 5. Seeker Preferences (`/seeker-preferences`)
| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `POST` | `/seeker-preferences` | Save roommate search preferences |
| `GET` | `/seeker-preferences?userId=:userId` | Fetch verified seekers with compatibility scores |
| `GET` | `/seeker-preferences/user/:userId` | Fetch preferences for a specific seeker |

### 6. Notifications (`/notifications`)
| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `POST` | `/notifications` | Create interest request or system notification |
| `GET` | `/notifications/:userId` | Fetch notifications for a user |
| `PATCH` | `/notifications/:id/read` | Mark individual notification as read |
| `PATCH` | `/notifications/user/:userId/read-all` | Mark all notifications as read |

### 7. Connection & Interest Requests (`/interests`)
| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `POST` | `/interests` | Send an interest request to a host/seeker |
| `PATCH` | `/interests/:id/status` | Accept or decline an interest request (`status: 'accepted' \| 'declined'`) |
| `GET` | `/interests/received/:userId` | Fetch received interest requests with sender details |
| `GET` | `/interests/sent/:userId` | Fetch sent interest requests with status |

### 8. Admin (`/admin`)
| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `POST` | `/admin/login` | Secure admin portal login |
| `GET` | `/admin/stats` | Retrieve platform KPI metrics |
| `GET` | `/admin/users` | List all users with filter/search |
| `PATCH` | `/admin/users/:userId/block` | Toggle block/unblock status |
| `PATCH` | `/admin/users/:userId/verify-identity` | Approve or reject identity documents |

---

## ⚡ Performance & Database Optimizations

1. **MongoDB Automatic TTL Purge**:
   - `OtpModel` utilizes `{ expires: 600 }` on `createdAt`. MongoDB's background index manager removes expired OTPs automatically without requiring cron jobs.
2. **Database Indexing**:
   - Unique lowercase index on `UserModel.email` for $O(1)$ lookup performance.
   - Foreign-key indexes on `userId` in `RoomModel`, `SeekerPreferenceModel`, and `NotificationModel` preventing slow $O(N)$ full-collection table scans.
3. **Mass-Assignment Security Guard**:
   - `MongoUserRepository` strictly enforces `PROFILE_UPDATABLE_FIELDS` to ensure users cannot elevate privileges (e.g. updating `isAdmin` or `isBlocked`).
4. **Cloudinary CDN Image Offloading**:
   - Base64 payload images are uploaded directly to Cloudinary CDN, keeping MongoDB document sizes minimal and queries fast.
5. **Decoupled Architecture**:
   - Presentation, Domain, Application, and Infrastructure layers are strictly isolated, enabling unit testing of business rules without booting Express or MongoDB.

